      "notes": "The verdict is well-structured and appropriately cautious. The too-uncertain direction is genuinely warranted: no provided evidence directly measures O15 indicators (social trust, belonging, inter-group relations, loneliness) following STV adoption. The crux_parameter and estimate_range are substantive, not lazy hedges. All claims are tier-appropriate \u2014 E10's 'expected to increase' is correctly labelled projected; E11 and E30 are measurable baselines. The E30 claim (60% support PR) is used only to note perceived legitimacy of current system, which is a reasonable inference from the quote without overstating. The E16 (positive campaigning) claim from makevotesmatter.org.uk is advocacy but is labelled projected and not the sole basis for any verdict. Rationale is party-blind and mechanism-focused. No lever leakage \u2014 the verdict explicitly declines to score electoral reform as a good in itself and routes only through O15 indicators. No false balance issue \u2014 the mixed/too-uncertain call is supported by genuine absence of O15-level evidence on both the positive and negative sides."
    },
